  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Pat draws a picture at the table. May sits next to him. \"I draw my toys,\" says Pat. \"Where is the robot?\" asks May. \"It is on the bed,\" says Pat. \"What color is it?\" asks May. \"It is gray.\" Pat draws a gray robot on the bed. \"Where is the train?\" asks May. \"It is next to the bed.\" Pat draws a red train.",
      "\"Where is the crocodile?\" asks May. \"It is in the box,\" says Pat. He draws a green crocodile. \"And the teddy?\" asks May. \"It is brown,\" says Pat. He looks at his crayons. He has no brown crayon. Pat is sad. \"I have a brown crayon,\" says May. \"Here you are.\" \"Thank you!\" says Pat.",
      "Pat draws the brown teddy. He draws a small brown dog, too. \"Who is the dog?\" asks May. \"It is Pip!\" says Pat. Pip comes and looks at the picture. \"Woof!\" says Pip. \"Pip is next to the red train,\" says Pat. May smiles. \"Draw me, too, Pat!\" says May."
    ],
    "summary": "Pat draws a picture of his toys, and May asks where they are and what color they are. May gives Pat a brown crayon, and Pat draws Pip.",
